Text: Constitution of the Republic of Iceland (No. 33, 17 June 1944, as amended to 24 June 1999), English translation published by the Prime Minister's Office on www.government.is. The site states that its content "may be freely used by everyone. Users are kindly requested to acknowledge their source." Source: Government of Iceland, Prime Minister's Office (https://www.government.is/topics/governance-and-national-symbols/constitution/). The translation is not the authentic text.

Text: The General Penal Code, No. 19/1940, English translation published by the Ministry of Justice of Iceland and hosted on www.ministryoffinance.is (https://www.ministryoffinance.is/library/01-Ministries/Ministry-of-Justice/Generlal%20Penal%20Code,%20No.19%201940.pdf), as amended up to Act 141/2018. The Government of Iceland's sites allow free use with acknowledgement of the source. The translation is not the authentic text.

Text: Act respecting Public Limited Companies, No. 2/1995, as amended up to 1 May 2011, English translation published on www.government.is (https://www.government.is/library/04-Legislation/Act%20No%202-1995.pdf). Free use with acknowledgement of the source. The original Icelandic text, as published in the Law Gazette (Stjórnartíðindi), is authoritative.

Text: Act on contracts, agency and void legal instruments, No. 7/1936, as amended up to Act 108/2006, English translation published by the Government of Iceland on www.stjornarradid.is (https://www.stjornarradid.is/media/atvinnuvegaraduneyti-media/media/acrobat/samningalog_tyddaensku.doc). Free use with acknowledgement of the source. The translation is not the authentic text; the Icelandic text governs.

Text (Icelandic acts): the editions of Lagasafn, the consolidated law collection published by the Althingi (https://www.althingi.is/lagasafn/), read from Internet Archive copies. Icelandic laws are not protected by copyright: Höfundalög nr. 73/1972, 9. gr.: "Lög, reglugerðir, fyrirmæli stjórnvalda, dómar og önnur áþekk gögn, sem gerð eru af opinberri hálfu, njóta ekki verndar eftir lögum þessum, og ekki heldur opinberar þýðingar á slíkum gögnum." The text authenticated in Stjórnartíðindi governs.

